Description:

Adds HTTP/3 (RFC 9114) support to httpd, served by a proto="quic"
service, including WebSockets over HTTP/3 (RFC 9220) and, with
http_allow_0rtt, 0-RTT early data.

To support it, master can now dispatch QUIC services, giving each
connection its own worker as it does for TCP.  By default master relays
a connection's packets to its worker; with quic_use_ebpf, an eBPF
SK_REUSEPORT program steers them to the worker directly.  The QUIC
transport (imap/quic.c, QUIC v1 and v2) is independent of HTTP/3.

While a QUIC service has at least half its maxchild workers busy,
master makes a new connection prove its address with a Retry before
giving it a worker (quic_retry), so a flood of Initials from forged
addresses can't tie up the workers.


Documentation:

docsrc/concepts/features/quic-dispatch.rst


Config changes:

New cyrus.conf service types: proto="quic", "quic4" and "quic6".

New imapoptions: http_h3_altsvc, quic_retry, quic_use_ebpf.

httptimeout, websocket_timeout and http_allow_0rtt now also apply to
HTTP/3 services.

New configure options: --disable-quic, --without-ngtcp2,
--without-nghttp3 and --without-quic-ebpf.


Upgrade instructions:

Opt-in: add a proto="quic" httpd service to cyrus.conf.  Requires
ngtcp2 and nghttp3, built against OpenSSL 3.5 or later.  The eBPF
backend also needs libbpf, libcap, clang and Linux 5.8, and master then
keeps CAP_BPF, CAP_NET_ADMIN, CAP_PERFMON and CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE for
its whole life.

quic_retry's default, "load", only takes effect on a service with a
maxchild limit.


